    {
      "text": "You can add user attributes or import them using a CSV file. You can add up to 128 attributes."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Adding a User Attribute",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To add a user attribute:"
    },
    {
      "item": "From the navigation menu, go to Administration > Authentication > Attributes.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          32,
          46
        ],
        [
          49,
          63
        ],
        [
          66,
          76
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the User Attribute tab, click Add Attribute.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          21
        ],
        [
          33,
          46
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "The Add Attribute drawer appears.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          17
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Add Attribute drawer:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          20
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute Name: Enter the name of the attribute that is required to be mapped to an external IdP (e.g., Manager or Organization).",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          14
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Display Name: Enter the display name for the attribute.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          12
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Description: Enter a description for the attribute.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          11
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Data Type: Select the type of data (String, Integer, Boolean, Date, or Decimal) the user needs to enter for this attribute.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          9
        ],
        [
          36,
          42
        ],
        [
          44,
          51
        ],
        [
          53,
          60
        ],
        [
          62,
          66
        ],
        [
          71,
          78
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Attribute Required: Select to mandate the attribute information when adding a user.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          18
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Save.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Importing a CSV File",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "You can add multiple user attributes to Authentication Service by importing a CSV file."
    },
    {
      "text": "To import a CSV file that contains a list of user attributes:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Go to Administration > Authentication > Attributes.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          20
        ],
        [
          23,
          37
        ],
        [
          40,
          50
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the User Attribute tab, click Import CSV.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          21
        ],
        [
          33,
          43
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "The Import Attributes window appears.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          21
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Import Attributes window, click the Download Sample link to download a sample CSV file.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          24
        ],
        [
          43,
          58
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Add the user attributes to the CSV file and save it in your local folder.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Import Attributes window, click Browse File to locate and upload the saved CSV file.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          24
        ],
        [
          39,
          50
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "If you want to replace the existing list of user attributes, select the Override Existing Entries checkbox.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 6,
      "strong": [
        [
          72,
          97
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Import.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 7,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          12
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The records are displayed in the Import Attributes window.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          33,
          50
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Review the list, then click Close.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 8,
      "strong": [
        [
          28,
          33
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The attributes are displayed on the User Attributes tab.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          36,
